cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "OrbitTrace: discovery of a recurrent late-April meteor-stream candidate in Global Meteor Network trajectories"
message: "If you use this repository, please cite the archived software/data release and the associated paper when available."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Li
    given-names: Brandon
    affiliation: "John L. Miller Great Neck North High School"
    email: brandon.li.gn@gmail.com
version: "1.0.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/brandonlign/orbittrace"
abstract: >-
  Code and derived data for OrbitTrace, a recurrent late-April meteor-stream
  candidate found in Global Meteor Network trajectories. The release includes
  the ACRF implementation, versioned analysis tables and results, benchmark
  summaries, and scripts for the paper figures. Source catalogues are not
  redistributed; their locations and acquisition details are documented in the
  repository.
keywords:
  - meteors
  - meteor streams
  - Global Meteor Network
  - reproducibility
